    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d288">

                <pb facs="0414" n="322" sameAs="frus:frus1899/pg322"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Sir Julian Pauncefote
                        to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >British Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1899-03-22"><hi rendition="#italic">March 22,
                        1899</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note No. 1381, of March 20, 1899, containing proposals for establishing
                    a provisional boundary line between Canada and the Territory of Alaska in the
                    region about the head of Lynn Canal without prejudice to the claims of either
                    party in the permanent adjustment of the frontier.</p>
                <p>I lost no time in communicating a copy of this note to Her Majesty’s Government
                    and to the Governor-General of Canada.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Julian
                    Pauncefote.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
